# `corpus` WAS IGNORED HERE, which is cargo-fuzz's default and wrong for
# this arrangement. The corpus is not scratch that a run regenerates: it
# is the seeds tests/fuzz_decoders.rs replays and mutates on every pull
# request, and the reproducer for every defect ever found. Ignoring it
# means the gate has nothing to run and the explorer starts from zero
# every night.
#
# scripts/fuzz-all.sh gives libFuzzer a throwaway directory to write its
# own discoveries into, so a local run does not fill this one with
# hash-named blobs.
